\0
After the Imperium's success in impersonating Freedom Guard forces on Lycean, the Imperium determined to create an entire division of fake Freedom Guard troops. To make the counterfeit forces more authentic, thousands of Imperium soldiers were injected with the Marked enzyme keys so that they would bear the Mark and be indistinguishable from genuine Freedom Guard units. Imperium researchers on Ternalin developed an agent to counteract the effects of the Marking for their troops.\n\n
The geneticist responsible for formulating the antidote, Gil Karoch, was working for the Imperium against his will. He leaked a small portion of the counter-agent to the Freedom Guard in the hope that they would be able to end their genetic bondage. However, Freedom Guard scientists were unable to duplicate the compound, and the Synod decided to attack Ternalin in an attempt to capture Karoch.
\1
The Freedom Guard has taken the Genetic Research Facility and captured Karoch. However, they have been unable to move him off of the planet. Retake the Facility and seize Karoch. A cruiser fleet is coming to move Karoch from Ternalin. Move him to the Off-World Transport Platform for evacuation before the fleet reaches Ternalin's orbit.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
-->  Recapture Karoch from the Freedom Guard\n
-->  Move Karoch to the Off-World Transport \n
\s\s\s\sPlatform before the fleet arrives
\2
The future of many is on your shoulders, but you are demonstrating that you are up to the challenge.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
Imperium forces on Ternalin withstood a massive Freedom Guard attack and prevented the Freedom Guard from successfully evacuating Karoch. Shortly after the battle, Imperium intelligence learned that Karoch had attempted to hand over the Mark counter-agent to the Freedom Guard, and he was executed.
\3
This does not bode well.
